KG42.register("clusters-920891ee7caff52e9e193329",{"id":"34-market_versus_price_scheduling::v142-d-CL001","paper":"34-market_versus_price_scheduling","label":"DMO customer participation and the scope of energy products","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL001","label":"DMO customer participation and the scope of energy products","market_meaning":"In the market-based model of this paper, the DMO provides end customers with a platform for participation in the energy market. The microgrids covered by the study are limited to private microgrids, and other responsive loads may optionally be included in the Customer layer. The ownership restriction applies only to the research scope of the microgrids.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["participation","bidding"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The private-microgrid restriction, end-customer participation, and the description of energy products belong to the same model. Other responsive loads are an optional extension. The microgrid ownership restriction cannot be extended to all customers, and the research scope of the paper cannot be elevated to a universal regulatory admission rule.","assembly_status":"assembled","boundary_rationale":"A scope-level procedural rule is formed from the participating objects, the participation activity provided by the DMO, and the energy products exchanged. Bid allocation, pricing, and deviation charges each have independent decision outcomes and are assembled separately.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"Provides the ownership research scope of the microgrid subclass and retains its character as a model condition."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R007","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Gives the DMO's responsibility to support end-customer participation and the optional scope of other responsive loads."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R009","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"Identifies the energy-trading products recorded by the existing chains of this cluster, and does not expand the product graph on this basis."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON001","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e015","v141-b-g01-e008","v141-b-g01-e012"],"rationale":"The private-microgrid research restriction and the scope of DMO customer participation are complementary. This mapping restricts only the microgrid subclass within that scope and does not assert that all customers must satisfy the private-microgrid condition."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON002","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e008"],"rationale":"The citation explicitly places end-customer market activity and customer-facing energy exchange on the same DMO platform. This supports complementarity between the participation function and the product scope, rather than duplication of two constraints."}],"object_mappings":[],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-G001","category":"unverified_source","description":"This cluster relies only on candidate citations whose use is permitted by the experiment. The related B records remain unverified, and no independent source audit has been performed.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R007","v141-c-R009"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e015","v141-b-g01-e008","v141-b-g01-e012"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Subsequently check the original-page transcription, the restricted objects, and the context. The assembly in this round does not mean that the source or the scientific content has received independent endorsement."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G002","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The R001 source restricts ownership to private ownership, whereas the framework definition of admission.local_area emphasizes geographic or feeder eligibility. The current attachment cannot prove that a geographic admission condition exists.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::admission.local_area","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e015"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream is to check the semantic fit between the ownership research condition and the existing admission node. If adjustment is needed, it is to proceed separately through a formal graph or ontology revision. The current objects remain frozen."}]},"rule_refs":["34-market_versus_price_scheduling::v141-c-R001","34-market_versus_price_scheduling::v141-c-R007","34-market_versus_price_scheduling::v141-c-R009"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-6d8bad3dd3b1de11","COMP-7f5e3dcddfa1014c","KG40-f19328f0aeb3d626","KG40-fe5714e5a1d65999"]});
